---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url, img } from '../../lib';
---
<Base title="About the designer" description="About Annika Palermo, a couture bridal designer (sample site; fictional biography).">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About the designer</p>
        <h1>Annika Palermo</h1>
        <p class="lead">Annika designs gowns the way a tailor builds a jacket: structure first, so the beauty can be effortless.</p>
        <p>Trained in patternmaking and couture finishing, she opened her studio to make a small number of made-to-measure gowns each season. Every commission is drafted for one bride, fitted in muslin, and cut and sewn in the studio.</p>
        <p>Her work moves between quiet minimalism (bias-cut crepe, clean necklines) and romantic construction: hand-placed lace, corsetry and tulle.</p>
        <p class="muted">This is a sample website. The biography, gowns and posts are fictional.</p>
      </div>
      <figure><img src={img('sketch.svg')} alt="Pencil-style illustration of a gown sketch from the studio" width="400" height="560"></figure>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The process</p>
      <h2>How a commission unfolds</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Consultation.</strong> We talk about the day, the venue and how you want to feel, and sketch together.</li>
        <li><strong>Design and fabric.</strong> A finished sketch and a box of swatches: silks, laces and tulles to touch.</li>
        <li><strong>Toile fittings.</strong> Two or three muslin fittings to perfect the fit before any final fabric is cut.</li>
        <li><strong>Construction.</strong> The gown is cut, sewn and finished by hand in the studio.</li>
        <li><strong>Final fitting.</strong> A last fitting and pressing, two weeks before the wedding.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a class="button solid" href={url('/contact/')}>Book a consultation</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
